      "title": "Note: Depth to Image (Iris-Z small)",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Depth to Image (Iris-Z small)\n\nA new picture on the layout of a depth map: what is near stays near, what is far stays far, and the prompt says\nwhat everything is. Iris-Z small is FLUX.2 Klein base 9B trained to make pictures and depth maps together; here\nthe depth map is given and it draws the picture.\n\n**Depth map** → **Iris-Z Depth Encode** → **VAE Encode** → reference latent on both prompts → 50 euler steps,\nCFG 4 → **VAE Decode** → `output/image/iris_z_from_depth_...`.\n\nThe sample depth map is the taxi photo's depth from Image to Depth (Iris-Z small).\n\n## Settings worth knowing\n\n- **Iris-Z Depth Encode, depth_format**: *disparity* for the depth maps of Depth Anything, Lotus or MoGe here\n  (bright = near), *depth* for bright = far, *Iris-Z depth* or *Iris-Z colours* for Image to Depth's outputs.\n- **Iris-Z Depth Encode, resolution**: 1024 (or 512): the picture has about that many pixels squared, in the depth\n  map's aspect; small maps are enlarged.\n- **CFG Guider, cfg**: 4, Iris-Z small's own default. The negative prompt stays empty, as Iris-Z was trained.\n- **Load LoRA (optional)**: bypassed. A FLUX.2 Klein 9B LoRA may load here; Iris-Z was fine-tuned from Klein base\n  9B, so the effect is not guaranteed.\n- Time: about 5 minutes the first time at 1024, about 4 once the models are loaded.\n## Model Links\n\n**diffusion_models/iris-z-small** (from [speridlabs/iris-z](https://huggingface.co/speridlabs/iris-z), folder `Iris-Z-small`, revision 5d35ec0)\n\n- transformer-00001-of-00004.safetensors to transformer-00004-of-00004.safetensors (18.2 GB, bf16)\n- empty_prompt.safetensors (13 MB)\n\n**vae**\n\n- [flux2-vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-klein/resolve/main/split_files/vae/flux2-vae.safetensors) (336 MB)\n\n**text_encoders**\n\n- [qwen_3_8b_fp8mixed.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-klein-9B/resolve/1138ce884c8e977cdacacbe779784fec4426bb3f/split_files/text_encoders/qwen_3_8b_fp8mixed.safetensors) (8.7 GB)\n\n## Where this workflow comes from\n\nOur own graph. Iris-Z is Speridlabs' FLUX.2 Klein base 9B trained to make a picture and its depth map together\n(arXiv 2611.16010). This pack's `iris_z_nodes.py` runs it on ComfyUI core's FLUX.2 model and sampler, written anew\nfrom the Iris-Z SDK (Apache-2.0); one model call matches the SDK's to bf16 rounding. The weights are under the FLUX\nnon-commercial licence: fine for personal and teaching use, not for commercial use. No licence to accept first."
      ]
    }
